<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">ʻAhoʻeitu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 950</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Aho'eitu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">ʻAhoʻeitu is the first Tuʻi Tonga, the sacred king of Tonga, in Tongan tradition, usually placed around the 10th century. The story makes him the son of the sky god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagaloa">Tangaloa</a> ʻEitumatupuʻa and a mortal woman, Ilaheva Vaʻepopua. Visiting his father in the sky, he was killed by jealous half-brothers and brought back to life, and was then sent down to rule Tonga, founding the line of Tuʻi Tonga that lasted until 1865.</p></div>
